    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 12,
    "summary": "Nathan tells David the parable of the ewe lamb—The Lord gave many wives to David, who is now cursed for taking Bathsheba—David fasts and prays for his son, but the Lord takes him—Solomon is born—David conquers the royal city of the Ammonites.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And the Lord sent Nathan unto David. And he came unto him, and said unto him, There were two men in one city; the one rich, and the other poor.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "2 Sam. 7:4 (2–17); 2 Chr. 29:25."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 12:1",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 12,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "The rich man had exceeding many flocks and herds:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 12
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 12:2",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 12,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "But the poor man had nothing, save one little ewe lamb, which he had bought and nourished up: and it grew up together with him, and with his children; it did eat of his own meat, and drank of his own cup, and lay in his bosom, and was unto him as a daughter.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 16
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 12:3",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 12,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And there came a traveller unto the rich man, and he spared to take of his own flock and of his own herd, to dress for the wayfaring man that was come unto him; but took the poor man’s lamb, and dressed it for the man that was come to him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 12:4",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 12,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And David’s anger was greatly kindled against the man; and he said to Nathan, As the Lord liveth, the man that hath done this thing shall surely die:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 80
          },
          {
            "start": 126,
            "end": 131
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 12:5",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 12,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
